{{!-- One writer's face, in the writer's own context.

	{{> "authors/portrait" size="h-24 w-24" px="96" textSize="text-2xl" defer=true}}   a masthead row or card
	{{> "authors/portrait" size="h-[132px] w-[132px]" px="132" textSize="text-4xl" extra="mx-auto mt-9"}}
	                                                                                   the A1 profile
	{{> "authors/portrait" size="h-28 w-28" px="112" textSize="text-3xl"}}             the A2 rail

	size       the box, as Tailwind utilities
	px         the same box in pixels, for the width/height attributes
	textSize   the initial's type size when there is no photograph
	extra      positioning utilities the call site adds
	defer      `loading="lazy" decoding="async"`, for the faces in a long list

Distinct from post/avatar.hbs, which draws the small unbordered badge a byline carries. The author
Surfaces draw a bordered circle cropped at `object-[50%_22%]` — the design's own crop, which keeps
a head in frame rather than centring on a chest — and that treatment is the whole reason this is a
second partial rather than an argument on the first.

`defer` IS OFF BY DEFAULT, and that is not a performance oversight. Both attributes tell the
browser it may paint a frame without the image, and a headless screenshot takes that permission —
which is what made two captures of the same post Surface differ by exactly the two avatars on it.
A profile portrait is the Surface's own subject, above the fold, and is never deferred; the
directories pass `defer=true` because their faces are a list that runs past the viewport, which is
what the design source marks lazy too.

A writer with no uploaded photograph gets the tinted initial, the same fallback and the same
one-letter concession recorded for post/avatar.hbs: Handlebars cannot take a substring and Ghost
ships no helper that can, so `{{name.[0]}}` is the whole of what is available. The badge carries
the border the photograph has, because in a row of five faces one circle without an outline reads
as a rendering fault rather than as a missing picture. --}}
{{#if profile_image}}
	<img
		src="{{img_url profile_image size="s"}}"
		alt="{{t "Portrait of {name}" name=name}}"
		width="{{px}}"
		height="{{px}}"
		{{#if defer}}loading="lazy" decoding="async"{{/if}}
		class="border-border {{size}} {{extra}} block rounded-full border object-cover object-[50%_22%]">
{{else}}
	<span
		aria-hidden="true"
		class="border-border bg-accent-soft font-ui text-accent-strong {{size}} {{extra}} {{textSize}} grid place-items-center rounded-full border font-semibold">{{name.[0]}}</span>
{{/if}}
